  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Light for «رحمة». The angels who record (21:18-22) are text only, never drawn. As-Sa'di's «فإن المكر السيئ لا يحيق إلا بأهله» (35:43) and Al-Muyassar's first-person «حفظتنا» are not used. STAGING v4: Staged in a market by day: two small groups of three men (blamed, so no woman is drawn). The second group walks in on 21:1. The left group sits, then rises on 21:4 under a light plate for the mercy after hardship (ease after hardship, Al-Muyassar; wealth after poverty among As-Sa'di's examples); on 21:9 and 21:11 the two groups talk to each other (their scheming against the signs; the gloss frames it). 21:14-17 is commanded to the Prophet: camera only, no gesture and no plate. The recording angels (21:19-22) are never drawn and no motif stands for their writing; the camera closes on the schemers on 21:22. The cover now shows the two groups talking (21:11)."
